{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376995-sleepers-using-charms","id":1376995,"title":"Sleepers Using Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-28T14:32:38-07:00","id":1376995,"title":"Sleepers Using Charms","content":"In the Book of Secrets, it mentions that paradox associated with vulgar effect charms would go to the user. Am I correct that a sleeper would therefore get a point of paradox for a successful use of a vulgar effect, i.e., from the charm? Would the backlash happen immediately, or would that be reserved for only a large accumulation of paradox per M20 (i.e., 5 points or more in a single go)?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","user":"Trategos_Sol","date":". 03-28-2020, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T13:31:25-07:00","id":1377221,"title":"","content":"I would say that, to the extent the sleeper can use the charm in the first place, then yes. However, I think the user has to have bought into the paradigm (to <i>some </i>degree) of the person who made the charm in the first place--but then you gotta wonder, if a regular person bought into a mage's paradigm to any degree (and therefore their construction of How Reality Works), how much of a sleeper are they actually?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T14:49:34-07:00","id":1377228,"title":"","content":"The answer does seem to have to be yes, even if Sleepers getting hit with Paradox is pretty pointless. It seems like a pretty rare situation (maybe to the point where it's not supposed to happen). A Sleeper can't use a Charm they'd generate Paradox for witnessing, and of course are automatically a witness as the person doing it.<br /> <br /> It seems like the intention is that Sleepers are really only going to end up using Charms that are coincidental within at least their local Reality Zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T15:28:25-07:00","id":1377231,"title":"","content":"The official rule on it is:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Mystic allies, meanwhile, can employ Charms\u2026 and a suitable impressionable Sleeper can use them too if she spends a point of Willpower, although a Sleeper whose disbelief would trigger Paradox cannot. <br /> <br /> <b>Book of Secrets</b> p.140</div>So honest-to-goodness, dyed-in-the-wool Sleepers never have to worry about what happens with Paradox accumulation, because if there would be any Paradox generated at all, the Charm simply fails. <br /> <br /> Things get slightly messier when you consider Extraordinary Citizens and their mystical counterparts: these are people who would otherwise qualify as Sleepers, except that they don't count as Witnesses to technomancy (in the case of Extraordinary Citizens) or to mystical phenomena (in the case of their mystical counterparts). They'd fall under the \u201cmystic allies\u201d of the above excerpt, letting them use appropriate Charms (even ones with Vulgar effects) without having to expend Willpower, at the cost of taking on the Paradox themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T15:41:13-07:00","id":1377233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376995-sleepers-using-charms?p=1377231#post1377231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So honest-to-goodness, dyed-in-the-wool Sleepers never have to worry about what happens with Paradox accumulation, because if there would be any Paradox generated at all, the Charm simply fails.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my first impression (and might be the intention), but I reversed when I considered the reading.<br /> <br /> BoS says, &quot;whose disbelief would trigger Paradox,&quot; not if Paradox gets generated. If, however narrow the circumstances, the Sleeper uses a Charm that fits their beliefs enough to not cause Paradox, but is vulgar and still generates Paradox, then this clause from the rules wouldn't apply.<br /> <br /> So, lets say a Sleeper in-the-dark Technocrat agent has a Charm that they're planting to spy on some Tradition mages. In normal Consensus reality, it's a coincidental Charm and there's no real problem with this. It's secret high tech spy shit they just need to hide somewhere as far as the Sleeper is concerned. However, they end up sneaking into a highly anti-tech Sanctum where the Reality Zone flips and now that Charm is vulgar.<br /> <br /> As written, the Sleeper can still try to plant the device and it will work (their belief isn't a problem) but it would be vulgar and automatically generate some Paradox for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T18:47:40-07:00","id":1377255,"title":"","content":"If it helps:<br /> <br /> The situation is an Imbued who now is in possession of magical bullets (the charms) and the corresponding gun from a Mage they thought was their ally. Now it is clear that the Mage is an adversary, and they are thinking of using the gun against them in the future. A Hunter is definitely not Awakened, knows that the supernatural exist, and has a gun (quite in line with their worldview) with bullets that they know are magical (they are clearing marked with sigils and vibrant).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T19:27:20-07:00","id":1377261,"title":"","content":"Ooh; an Imbued, huh? How strict are the Messengers? I ask because some of the early material for HtR made a point that supernatural powers other than the Edges that the Imbued receive through their Virtues are completely verboten to the Imbued. If that's the case, then your Hunter character will count as a Sleeper who doesn't have the right mindset to qualify to activate the bullet Charms. If he can't trigger the magic in the bullets, the issue of what happens when the bullets are activated becomes moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T20:02:32-07:00","id":1377267,"title":"","content":"If the Imbued character thinks the bullets will work - really believes in their efficacy - they shouldn't have any problem using them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T14:31:51-07:00","id":1377394,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd treat the Imbued like any of the other supernatural splats with regard to Paradox, e.g. not a sleeper and doesn't count as a witness for vulgar Effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T15:15:18-07:00","id":1377400,"title":"","content":"Except that the whole point of the Imbued was \u201cbut we're <i>not</i> Soopernatural! Honest!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T16:30:54-07:00","id":1377407,"title":"","content":"Except no, that's not the &quot;whole point&quot; of the Imbued at all.<br /> <br /> There is a valid argument in whether or not magical items should work for the Imbued, but they don't count as Sleepers. It doesn't make sense from a Mage perspective, or a Hunter perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}